.TH MYSYSPILOT 1 "October 2026" "1.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mysyspilot \- Linux system optimizer, monitor, disk utility and speed test
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mysyspilot
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-browser ]
.RB [ \-\-new\-instance ]
.br
.B mysyspilot \-\-install\-desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mysyspilot
starts a local dashboard on 127.0.0.1 (default port 8787), protected by a
per\-launch token and a Host header check, and opens it in a browser app
window. If an instance of the same version is already running, the existing
window is reopened instead; an older running version is replaced.
.PP
Do not run it as root. Privileged actions are authorized per action through
polkit (pkexec or UDisks2).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
Listen port. A free port is chosen automatically if it is busy.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-browser
Do not open a window; print the URL instead.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-instance
Start a separate server even if one is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-desktop
Create a per\-user application menu launcher and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mysyspilot/
Per\-user data (mode 0700): speed test history, filesystem check status,
backup catalog, recovery undo logs and
.IR instance.json ,
which holds the port and session token of the running server (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/mysyspilot/msp\-diskhelper
Raw disk helper run as root through pkexec (polkit action
.IR com.mysyspilot.diskhelper ).
.SH NETWORK
There is no telemetry and no update check. Opening the Speed Test page
downloads the LibreSpeed server list (librespeed.org) and pings the listed
servers; running a test contacts the chosen server (Cloudflare or a
LibreSpeed server). APT, Snap, Flatpak and Docker operations contact their
configured repositories or registries.
